#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:65 515c96d576b14532a680798c09664cb6
msgid "**Name**: ``GTDB_get_species``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:67 fac1eb177d254bd99b44a750bcde2ac5
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get detailed information about a GTDB species cluster, "
"including all genomes assigned to that species. A GTDB species cluster "
"groups genomes by average nucleotide identity (ANI). Returns the full "
"list of genomes with their accessions, NCBI organism names, NCBI "
"taxonomy, and whether they are the GTDB species representative or NCBI "
"type material. Useful for exploring species diversity, finding "
"representative genomes, and comparing GTDB vs NCBI classifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:71 51fee47233374491a71afadadde269a1
msgid "``operation`` (string) (required) Operation type (fixed: get\\_species)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:74 98438a7c271b45c394530a78910a8bbe
msgid ""
"``species`` (string) (required) Species name WITHOUT the s\\_\\_ prefix "
"(e.g., 'Escherichia coli', 'Hydrogenothermus marinus', 'Bacillus "
"subtilis')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:77 670870a86f0c4a3c8a3fabf5955a4134
msgid ""
"``max_genomes`` (integer) (optional) Maximum number of genomes to return "
"(default: 20). Species clusters can have thousands of genomes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:95 61c70199014a46459e10642a051ef191
msgid "**GTDB_get_taxon_info** (Type: GTDBTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:97 3a0679838cd44b5291b51c2d7b58d7bd
msgid ""
"Get information about a GTDB taxon including its rank, total genome "
"count, higher-rank lineage, a..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst e831481a34c4422f87f692ebbd474672
msgid "GTDB_get_taxon_info tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:103 968375b88e764bf2a0a0df6ea08eeb4f
msgid "**Name**: ``GTDB_get_taxon_info``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:105 2673707abff54c73bc7253b4760db136
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get information about a GTDB taxon including its rank, "
"total genome count, higher-rank lineage, and release history. GTDB uses "
"rank prefixes: d\\_\\_ (domain), p\\_\\_ (phylum), c\\_\\_ (class), "
"o\\_\\_ (order), f\\_\\_ (family), g\\_\\_ (genus), s\\_\\_ (species). "
"For example, f\\_\\_Lachnospiraceae returns its rank (Family), genome "
"count, and lineage (Bacteria > Bacillota > Clostridia > Lachnospirales). "
"Also returns the full lineage breakdown from domain to species. Useful "
"for understanding where a taxon fits in the GTDB tree and how many "
"genomes support it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:109 2d3624a8ed7c4e74b8cfe86e5536478d
msgid ""
"``operation`` (string) (required) Operation type (fixed: "
"get\\_taxon\\_info)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:112 4d798dfc1e454a9e8a0a04f1d027d5fa
msgid ""
"``taxon`` (string) (required) GTDB taxon name with rank prefix (e.g., "
"'f\\_\\_Lachnospiraceae', 'd\\_\\_Bacteria', 'g\\_\\_Escherichia', "
"'s\\_\\_Escherichia coli'). Use GTDB\\_search\\_taxon to find valid "
"names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/gtdb_tools.rst:130 d89e6c8256e541079e1641fd240a2a2e
